{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast","id":1508831,"title":"Alpen, Mares, and Sleep Paralysis-Dream Metaphysics in Beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-18T21:14:33-07:00","id":1508831,"title":"Alpen, Mares, and Sleep Paralysis-Dream Metaphysics in Beast","content":"So, ever since I learned of Beast's relationship with dreams and Dreams, I've wondered what exactly happens when a Beast enters the Bastion. And what can they do to a dream for both the inside and the outside? Well, hopefully, this thread can sort that out. So this is also a continuation of a conversation started in the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project#post1508827\">Night Horrors: Scourging Thorns fan project </a>which you should check out/ help out with...you know, if you want.<br /> Here is the start of the conversation.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project#post1508827\">\u200b</a><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508813#post1508813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, so I\u2019ve thinking about what would happen to a Beast who enters a Bastion\u2026like a lot. Should I try and see what Beast Oneiromancy looks like?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508815#post1508815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which reminds me; by default, the dreams of the Dreaming Roads are \u2018real\u2019 dreams and not the metaphoric \u2018dreams\u2019 of the Astral/ ___<br /> Dream proper, so mundane Beasts shouldn\u2019t have much to do with fae oneiromancy.<br /> <br /> <br /> The operative words here being \u2018by default\u2019 and \u2018mundane\u2019, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508817#post1508817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It looks like Lair Imposition and Primordial Pathways. A Beast in a Bastion is like a changeling physically being in a Bastion, except that Beasts aren't kitted for manipulating dreams and instead use soulscapes like a hammer if resonance or Lair Traits are present. A Horror in a Bastion separate from the Beast has already accounted for it.<br /> <br /> The most pertinent questions as all this goes is &quot;Is a Bastion that is having Lair traits imposed or is otherwise interlapped with a Lair harder to manipulate for weird soul/dream metaphysical differential reasons or not?&quot;(I'd argue probably not, but I can see why someone might say otherwise) and &quot;Can Beasts develop soft dreamweaving abilities though kinship to Changelings?&quot;(I'd argue yeah, probably.)<br /> <br /> Dreams are a window into the soul, and visa versa, but there are reasons there are no standing rules for the Lost's ability to affect souls or for the Children's ability to affect dreams-they are different mediums, and the tools that each have are built to task and in accordance to each's nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508819#post1508819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right\u2026but what about the Nightmares that wait until the next sleep? How do those work from the inside?<br /> <br /> Edit: Should I take this conversation to the Beast forum? I don\u2019t want to derail the thread with Beast metaphysics when it\u2019s only going to be a small part of the project.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508820#post1508820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Admittedly a more interesting question I didn't account for. I'll have to wait till I can grab my copy of the BPG for a detailed answer, but off my head, though, that runs into a catch that Nightmares functionally plunge a soul/-equivalent* into the Primordial Dream. The dreams as they are in the Bastion (probably) don't much factor into it so much as the act of falling asleep is a good psychospiritual semiotic for what happens there.<br /> <br /> *Well, more the seat for the soul/-equivalent, given that souls aren't strictly the whole of a person's essence. Soulless people and monsters can be afflicted by Nightmares and all that jazz.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508824#post1508824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said (posting as a second post to not trigger the spam filter), given that Nightmares tend to wake when they're triggered, Bastions probably don't really get much of a chance to form and reflect the Nightmare-though if you have an exceptional situation where the Nightmare both triggers AND the victim can't wake up, the Bastion probably abruptly changes channels towards the repetition of the Nightmare's premise.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508826#post1508826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Homebrew off the top of my head, away from my pdfs atm: Supernatural powers that warp or key off dreams/sleep (not just Begotten Nightmares) are visible in the Bastion as, mostly, circumstances and environments. If the changeling visited the victim\u2019s dreams before, she\u2019ll recognize that something\u2019s not quite right. From there, the changeling can use oneiromancy to neutralize the power. It\u2019s still there, just ineffectively so (like what happens with Awakened spells that are Withstood). If the original user of the power somehow loses control over the power, it becomes an Eidolon and wrecks havoc. Sometimes, such Eidolons slip outside the Dreaming Roads and into the wider Hedge, becoming Night Horror-worthy monsters that are uncannily familiar with supernaturals that \u2018birthed\u2019 them.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-19-2023, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T21:31:13-07:00","id":1508832,"title":"","content":"Hopefully, this thread will cover: What exactly are dreams/Dreams in the Chronicles of Darkness setting, What happens when Changelings mess around in them, How does a Beast get into a Bastion, What does a Bastion feel like to a Beast, What are all the ways a Beast can interact with a Dream/Bastion, What do delayed Nightmares actually do to dreams, and finally, How does Changeling Kinship mess with all of this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-19-2023, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T21:58:36-07:00","id":1508833,"title":"","content":"So, as a baseline: what exactly is a dream in Chronicles? Well according to my understanding, it's a lot like what it is in real life. A hallucination where your brain processes all the stuff that happens to you through symbol and metaphor. Here's the thing, in Chronicles, that's connected to your soul, and through your soul, all souls. So, the usual metaphor is the branches of a Great Tree. dreams are leaves on a branch, spouting, budding, blooming, wilting, and fading away. The Branch itself is a person, usually a soul. That soul eventually connects to other souls to form a Trunk, which then trails down into the Soil and Earth, connecting a human soul to all other human souls, and eventually the souls of everything else. This is all called the Dreaming by Beasts and the Astral by Mages.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is where that metaphor breaks down because dreams are made semi-physical on the Dreaming Roads as Bastions. The Hedge is the Astral Barrier according to Mages, the in-between of the Waking World and the Dreaming, a mixture that is both and neither. The Hedge is a lot of other things besides, and for our purposes, I don't think it really matters, outside of Bastions being places on the Dreaming Roads being where dreams physically take place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-19-2023, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T22:02:31-07:00","id":1508834,"title":"","content":"If the Astral/Dream is the ocean, than dreams are the beaches. Such was the metaphor I remember picking up ages ago, and it seems to hold to this day. Beasts are creatures of the Dream, and have surprisingly little to do with dreams. (Note the capitalizations and the plurals!)<br /> <br /> That said, I imagine what Beasts do with dreams has more to do with feeding and Nightmares.<br /> <br /> IIRC, Starving Beasts\u2019 Horrors go out to feed themselves in the local Dream-scape. Maybe this happens in the local dream-scape instead, and such blurring of lines is one of the reasons why Beasts themselves don\u2019t bother to differentiate between dreams and the Dream/Astral. <br /> <br /> Hmm\u2026\u2026 IIRC, a piece of Mage material somewhere proposed that the soul-stinging Astral Threshold between the Oneiros and the Temenos may be the Hedge, or at least its entrance. (Maybe mages can learn to \u2018step sideways\u2019 from the Threshold and into the Hedge, much like how they can \u2018step sideways\u2019 from the Omphalos between the Temenos and Anima Mundi to reach the Primordial Dream?)<br /> (Then again, a fan theory I remember whose source I forgot posits that the Hedge may be related to the Abyss, further muddying the map\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T22:23:20-07:00","id":1508837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508834#post1508834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Astral/Dream is the ocean, than dreams are the beaches. Such was the metaphor I remember picking up ages ago, and it seems to hold to this day. Beasts are creatures of the Dream, and have surprisingly little to do with dreams. (Note the capitalizations and the plurals!)</div> </div> </div> </div> Dang it, yeah ok. I'll fix that. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Yeah, honestly that's what bugs me. Creatures of Dream should affect dreams too, and Beast basically never focused on it in any detail. But they do mess with dreams! Between Nightmares causing nightmares, Horrors going into dreams, and so many powers causing nightmares as a side effect, dream manipulation is clearly an element of Beast...that barely any word count is given to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508834#post1508834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I imagine what Beasts do with dreams has more to do with feeding and Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, that's one of the things I'm hoping this thread will sort out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508834#post1508834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, Starving Beasts\u2019 Horrors go out to feed themselves in the local Dream-scape. Maybe this happens in the local dream-scape instead, and such blurring of lines is one of the reasons why Beasts themselves don\u2019t bother to differentiate between dreams and the Dream/Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div> You are correct, the Horror Primordial Pathways into a resonant dream/Bastion to feed according to pg 22 of the Player's Guide to Contagion<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508834#post1508834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm\u2026\u2026 IIRC, a piece of Mage material somewhere proposed that the soul-stinging Astral Threshold between the Oneiros and the Temenos may be the Hedge, or at least its entrance. (Maybe mages can learn to \u2018step sideways\u2019 from the Threshold and into the Hedge, much like how they can \u2018step sideways\u2019 from the Omphalos between the Temenos and Anima Mundi to reach the Primordial Dream?)<br /> (Then again, a fan theory I remember whose source I forgot posits that the Hedge may be related to the Abyss, further muddying the map\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div> So here is the path as I understand, (and I could be very wrong!): Waking World&lt;-&gt;dreams=Bastion/Dreaming Roads/Hedge=Astral Barrier&lt;-&gt;Oneiros=Personal Dream&lt;-&gt;Temenos=Bright Dream&lt;-&gt;(The Day/Primordial Dream/The Mists)&lt;-&gt;The Cave/Omphalos&lt;-&gt;Anima Mundi/Mother's Land.<br /> <br /> Edit: The Primordial Dream is stated somewhere to be part of both the Temenos and the Anima Mundi, which is why it reflects the real world in its layout, and trauma can make new Chambers that still reflect the Waking World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-19-2023, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T22:52:53-07:00","id":1508839,"title":"","content":"So, next up, how do Changelings get to the Bastion and Dreamweave? Well, generally they just walk there, either physically through the Hedge, or Lucid Dream Walk out of their Bastion into a new one. And when they are in a new Bastion, they are interpreted as just another symbol playing out in the dream. Basically, they are given a role and are expected by the rest of the dream to act inside that role. And If they don't, the Dream and the inhabitants kinda just ignore them? (Not clear to me if simply not acting according to the role *is* dreamweaving or not) If they spend Glamor, their actions manipulate the symbol set the dream is working with, which it resists.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I just flagged my previous post, because I kept altering it to better fit what I understand of the actual layout of the Astral. Anyways the important point was that the Primordial Dream is in between the Bright Dream and the Mother's Land, Aka the Temenos and the Anima Mundi, and the Hedge would actually be in-between the Waking World and the Dreaming. Also, the Horror totally enters the Bastion as per pg 22 of Contagion Player's Guide","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-19-2023, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T23:59:06-07:00","id":1508850,"title":"","content":"Ok, but what about the Begotten? How do they get into Dreams? Well...They connect a resonant part of the Waking World to their Lair, walk to another chamber, and connect the Lair to a resonant dream. The Horror can do this too, it's how it feeds on people in the first place, and it has a better understanding of what dreams are available...somehow. (I think it might be because the resonant lair traits are part of its symbol set, and as a Quasi-Temonic entity, it knows when anyone has that symbol playing in their dreams.) So, to get someone specific, you need to get lucky...or set things up in advance. (more on that later) They notably will be physically in the dream, and emerge merged with the Horror. (Hmm, seems important, could determine what role a Beast is given.) That's pretty much it. Maybe, maybe a Beast could gain Kinship merit letting them step from the Personal Soul into the Bastion, and thus better target someone specific, but that's speculation right now.<br /> <br /> Edit: Under the Bed has a mention of appearing in someone's personal dreams before moving on to the Primordial Pathways. Interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-19-2023, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T00:09:36-07:00","id":1508851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508850#post1508850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Under the Bed has a mention of appearing in someone's personal dreams before moving on to the Primordial Pathways. Interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you make a freeway through someone's head, yer gonna see the gas station.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T00:14:12-07:00","id":1508853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508851#post1508851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you make a freeway through someone's head, yer gonna see the gas station.</div> </div> </div> </div>But can I make a off-ramp to stop at the gas station?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T00:14:34-07:00","id":1508854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508826#post1508826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Homebrew off the top of my head, away from my pdfs atm: Supernatural powers that warp or key off dreams/sleep (not just Begotten Nightmares) are visible in the Bastion as, mostly, circumstances and environments. If the changeling visited the victim\u2019s dreams before, she\u2019ll recognize that something\u2019s not quite right. From there, the changeling can use oneiromancy to neutralize the power. It\u2019s still there, just ineffectively so (like what happens with Awakened spells that are Withstood). If the original user of the power somehow loses control over the power, it becomes an Eidolon and wrecks havoc. Sometimes, such Eidolons slip outside the Dreaming Roads and into the wider Hedge, becoming Night Horror-worthy monsters that are uncannily familiar with supernaturals that \u2018birthed\u2019 them.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDirectly addressing this: Bastions only exist while a person is sleeping. Nightmares plunge the target's mind into the Primordial Dream, with the delay effect taking advantage of the psychospiritual semiotic of a person falling asleep as an effective metaphor for that. Usually, they wake up kicking and screaming as a result.<br /> <br /> So the catch to this read is this: How does one visit a Bastion that doesn't exist to do all of that?<br /> <br /> Short answer, they don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508853#post1508853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But can I make a off-ramp to stop at the gas station?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules as written? Nope.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T00:22:32-07:00","id":1508855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508854#post1508854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bDirectly addressing this: Bastions only exist while a person is sleeping. Nightmares plunge the target's mind into the Primordial Dream, with the delay effect taking advantage of the psychospiritual semiotic of a person falling asleep as an effective metaphor for that. Usually, they wake up kicking and screaming as a result.<br /> <br /> So the catch to this read is this: How does one visit a Bastion that doesn't exist to do all of that?<br /> <br /> Short answer, they don't.</div> </div> </div> </div> Usually the Nightmare has to play out before they wake, right? I mean, otherwise, why would they wake up? So, we do have a period of time before the Bastion is dissolved in the Dream. Maybe not long, but I've had dreams that seemed to be months when I was only asleep for a few hours. Is that enough wiggle room?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508854#post1508854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules as written? Nope.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'll come back to this when it's actually homebrew time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T00:41:09-07:00","id":1508858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508855#post1508855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Usually the Nightmare has to play out before they wake, right? I mean, otherwise, why would they wake up? So, we do have a period of time before the Bastion is dissolved in the Dream. Maybe not long, but I've had dreams that seemed to be months when I was only asleep for a few hours. Is that enough wiggle room?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To cite Beast:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Success: The Nightmare takes effect either immediately or when the victim next sleeps, as the Beast desires. If the victim is subject to multiple \u201cdormant\u201d Nightmares, he suffers one Nightmare each time he sleeps, in order of when the Nightmares were applied. </div> </div> </div>Now, we could quibble about what is meant by sleep, but in the spirit of the games, I'm going to run on the assumption that means when the brain is starting to dream. Which leads to the next citation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While Nightmares are \u201call in your head\u201d in the sense that only the victim experiences the effects and sees the hallucinations, that\u2019s not the same thing as Nightmares being \u201cillusionary\u201d or somehow \u201cnot real.\u201d The effects of Nightmares are very real and are quite capable of inflicting somatic injury or even death. Just because no one else can see the bugs crawling all over you doesn\u2019t mean they aren\u2019t there. </div> </div> </div>Why would you wake up? Because there are bugs eating your face. They may only be there for you, but they are there.<br /> <br /> Oneiromancy isn't enough to handle a Nightmare if it's already afflicted on a victim, though an oneiromancer may be able to creatively fortify the dreamer through dreams against attacks of Nightmares in advance. Contracts are more likely the actual realm of handling the sort of remediation you're looking for.<br /> <br /> Also, Bastions happen in the Hedge/Astral Barrier, not in the Dreaming/Astral, dreams/Bastions are not the Primordial Dream/The Dreaming in General/the Oneiros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-19-2023, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T00:57:52-07:00","id":1508860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508858#post1508858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To cite Beast:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, we could quibble about what is meant by sleep, but in the spirit of the games, I'm going to run on the assumption that means when the brain is starting to dream. Which leads to the next citation:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why would you wake up? Because there are bugs eating your face. They may only be there for you, but they are there.<br /> <br /> Oneiromancy isn't enough to handle a Nightmare if it's already afflicted on a victim, though an oneiromancer may be able to creatively fortify the dreamer through dreams against attacks of Nightmares in advance. Contracts are more likely the actual realm of handling the sort of remediation you're looking for.<br /> <br /> Also, Bastions happen in the Hedge/Astral Barrier, not in the Dreaming/Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we may have had a miscommunication, I'm not contesting any bit of that. I fully understand Nightmares will eventually wake you up. But I'm wonder if there is enough time if preplanned to do something like enter the Bastion while the symbol story of &quot;Bugs Eat your Face&quot; plays out. I mean, it plays out like a dream, yeah? It has a story, maybe a weird one to be sure, but there is a progression. Something like, walking along a trail, tripping, and then falling into a swarm of bugs. They crawl onto your face and chow down. Someone with the Swarms Lair trait could hypothetically enter while the swarm of bugs gathers and surge forward on one's face. How long do bugs eat a face before one wakes up? <br /> <br /> And I was being poetic with the last bit, it's just fancy talk for Nightmare wakes someone up. Not an actual statement of metaphysics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T01:06:52-07:00","id":1508861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508858#post1508858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, we could quibble about what is meant by sleep, but in the spirit of the games, I'm going to run on the assumption that means when the brain is starting to dream. Which leads to the next citation:</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually how do Nightmares hypothetically do this again? They work by working the Horror's symbolism into the symbolism used for dream for that night's sleep, right? Would it be within the scope of a merit to delay that process? Like the Bugs that Eat Your face are in the background...waiting. Until a predetermined symbol sets them off. Does that seem plausible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T01:25:34-07:00","id":1508864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508860#post1508860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we may have had a miscommunication, I'm not contesting any bit of that. I fully understand Nightmares will eventually wake you up. But I'm wonder if there is enough time if preplanned to do something like enter the Bastion while the symbol story of &quot;Bugs Eat your Face&quot; plays out. I mean, it plays out like a dream, yeah? It has a story, maybe a weird one to be sure, but there is a progression. Something like, walking along a trail, tripping, and then falling into a swarm of bugs. They crawl onto your face and chow down. Someone with the Swarms Lair trait could hypothetically enter while the swarm of bugs gathers and surge forward on one's face. How long do bugs eat a face before one wakes up?<br /> <br /> And I was being poetic with the last bit, it's just fancy talk for Nightmare wakes someone up. Not an actual statement of metaphysics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really! Bastions form when you start dreaming, Nightmares trigger when you fall asleep. Even at the most generous reading of both of those, the Nightmare triggers right when the Bastion starts forming, and unless a target has an exceptional reason to stay asleep, the personal reality of a Nightmare is going wake them up, and get them dealing with it as a real issue. The fight-or-flight instinct is a bitch to fight.<br /> <br /> Like, The most likely place of misunderstanding is that because both dreams and Nightmares play out in a victim's head, and we're used to thinking of the two as the same thing, there's an assumption that a Nightmare is a dream. It's not. To quote Nightmares from the core:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even creatures that don\u2019t dream or feel fear can tremble before the power of the Dark Mother. </div> </div> </div>Bastions are a space for dreams. Nightmares can affect things that don't dream. Two plus two. &quot;Plays out like a dream&quot; is not &quot;it is a dream.&quot; A Nightmare is not a three act play, it is &quot;your reality is bugs are eating your face.&quot;<br /> <br /> AT best, and I being very, <i>very </i>generous on this, if you could freeze or massively expand the period of time in which the Bastion would start forming and the Nightmare would start triggering*, you might be able to go and do shenanigans with that, but that's a niche of a niche, and thus the issue of a story and not business as usual. Hell, that's not the only way to force a person to for sure stay asleep while a nightmare is going off, but that's not going to facilitate the preventative aspect of this discussion.<br /> <br /> You can preplan for a Nightmare, and you can pretty reasonably create circumstances that force a Bastion to persist while a Nightmare plays out-but in the idea of the original post that led us here, there's no going into a Bastion to stop a Nightmare from happening, because pretty much none of this works that way. Bastions don't exist by the time the bad things start happening.<br /> <br /> *And I don't want to be a pedant on this, but if we wanna get clinical on this, you ABSOLUTELY fall asleep long before you start dreaming proper.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T01:50:58-07:00","id":1508867,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see. I was on the page of using Nightmares for Lair Resonance to enter, not to stop a Nightmare. I guess I didn't communicate that well. So I was under the assumption that the process goes:<br /> place Nightmare &gt; sleep&gt; REM starts&gt; Nightmare plays out in Dream &gt; Wake up because its a dream where bugs are eating you&gt; If nightmare hasn't run out of duration, is still going in a kinda waking dream&gt; duration ends<br /> <br /> If I understand you correctly it is more like:<br /> place Nightmare &gt; sleep&gt; REM starts&gt; Nightmare plays out in &quot;personal reality&quot;&gt; Wake up because the body says bugs are eating you, no not a joke or dream, wake up now&gt;duration ends<br /> <br /> Is that correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-19-2023, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T02:30:11-07:00","id":1508870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508854#post1508854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bDirectly addressing this: Bastions only exist while a person is sleeping. Nightmares plunge the target's mind into the Primordial Dream, with the delay effect taking advantage of the psychospiritual semiotic of a person falling asleep as an effective metaphor for that. Usually, they wake up kicking and screaming as a result.<br /> <br /> So the catch to this read is this: How does one visit a Bastion that doesn't exist to do all of that?<br /> <br /> Short answer, they don't.<br /> .\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, that\u2019s what happens when you homebrew without the pdfs open, as I said in that thread!<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, that thread was for Night Horrors \u2014 in that vein, I still think we have room for unique horrors precisely because of that \u201cWait, what?\u201d factor.<br /> Like, wasn\u2019 there this misogynistic/misandrist Insatiable (forgot which) that fed over the internet? (I\u2019m still away from my books\u2026) Things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T05:09:58-07:00","id":1508876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508834#post1508834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm\u2026\u2026 IIRC, a piece of Mage material somewhere proposed that the soul-stinging Astral Threshold between the Oneiros and the Temenos may be the Hedge, or at least its entrance. (Maybe mages can learn to \u2018step sideways\u2019 from the Threshold and into the Hedge, much like how they can \u2018step sideways\u2019 from the Omphalos between the Temenos and Anima Mundi to reach the Primordial Dream?)<br /> (Then again, a fan theory I remember whose source I forgot posits that the Hedge may be related to the Abyss, further muddying the map\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedge being interpreted by mages as the painful Astral Barrier they have to push through to enter the soul-realms proper is canon since Mysterious Frontiers in Dark Eras 2, which also carries forward the thematic association of the realm as crossing the Abyss (first posited in Imperial Mysteries as the reason the Old Gods of Thistle's labyrinth tears at the soul) with the fact that it can make your Mage Sight lie to you and use Paradoxes to give you Goblin Debt.<br /> <br /> Mages access the Primordial Dream like any other part of the Temenos, i.e. they follow thematic associations in a way that Beasts recognize as most analogous to using a Burrow until they enter a Lair and have to get out to stop treating it like normal space.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508837#post1508837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: The Primordial Dream is stated somewhere to be part of both the Temenos and the Anima Mundi, which is why it reflects the real world in its layout, and trauma can make new Chambers that still reflect the Waking World.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordial Dream is approximately flush with the Omphalos/the Cave, which is the shallowest layer of the Anima Mundi (the Ecstatic Wind hits once per day spent in there and if you're not a Beast or otherwise navigating without a solid division between the human- and world-souls you need to spend Mana to travel through the stone). The thinness of reality in the Dark Dream outside of Lairs and the fact that navigating the Bright Dream is specifically compared to Burrows (plus the fact that that sort of shortcut explicitly doesn't work in the Mother's Land) is generally the least awkward way to interpret the KS draft's statement of the Lair being between the two post-BPG; the dreamscape is otherwise roughly similar to the Gauntlet in being mostly a non-space between worlds, particularly once you get to the Mists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T21:22:41-07:00","id":1508989,"title":"","content":"So, Beasts can enter dreams, so what happens when they do? Well, this is the point where I really only have conjecture. A thing I find interesting and potentially relevant is that Beasts are increasingly uncomfortable the further they get from the Primordial Dream. The Personal Dream is described as being outright oppressive. I posit that Beasts aren't really &quot;meant&quot; to be in soul realms. The symbols press too closely and are too thin. It might be a bit like a deep ocean fish being brought to near-surface waters. So, what about dreams? Shouldn't they be even closer to the surface? This makes me think that dreams feel just plain wrong for Beasts to enter, like standing on thin ice. How does this manifest? Well, the dream forces Changelings to conform to a role, why not do the same for Beasts? And how would a person so closely linked to their personal narrative feel, to be interpreted as something completely different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-20-2023, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T23:43:53-07:00","id":1509005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1508989#post1508989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Beasts can enter dreams, so what happens when they do? Well, this is the point where I really only have conjecture. A thing I find interesting and potentially relevant is that Beasts are increasingly uncomfortable the further they get from the Primordial Dream. The Personal Dream is described as being outright oppressive. I posit that Beasts aren't really &quot;meant&quot; to be in soul realms. The symbols press too closely and are too thin. It might be a bit like a deep ocean fish being brought to near-surface waters. So, what about dreams? Shouldn't they be even closer to the surface? This makes me think that dreams feel just plain wrong for Beasts to enter, like standing on thin ice. How does this manifest? Well, the dream forces Changelings to conform to a role, why not do the same for Beasts? And how would a person so closely linked to their personal narrative feel, to be interpreted as something completely different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation needed? For...all of that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T23:54:13-07:00","id":1509006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509005#post1509005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Citation needed? For...all of that?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BPG pg 153</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIf the press of the shared realms is claustrophobic, these individual realms are downright oppressive to a Beast \u2014 travelers feel like they are under constant, deep scrutiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>The forced assumption of the role is actually wrong, as per<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL 2e core pg 218</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A changeling oneiropomp must engage directly with the ongoing scene within the dream before she can make changes or glean secrets, and she must take up a role that matches what\u2019s already happening there when she arrives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess I misremembered.<br /> <br /> The rest is speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T00:59:27-07:00","id":1509008,"title":"","content":"Okay, the problem was not that I misremembered, it's that I misread you.<br /> <br /> but, like. I need to go to bed, but.<br /> <br /> Your conclusion for moving from sparely populated soulspaces to a very populated soulspace is that they're not meant for soul realms?<br /> <br /> Cause it's a density thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T08:54:44-07:00","id":1509040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509008#post1509008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, the problem was not that I misremembered, it's that I misread you.<br /> <br /> but, like. I need to go to bed, but.<br /> <br /> Your conclusion for moving from sparely populated soulspaces to a very populated soulspace is that they're not meant for soul realms?<br /> <br /> Cause it's a density thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t remember mages having that issue in other people\u2019s personal dream. Could be wrong, but I figured it might that be because Beasts were more in tune with the Primordial Dream as their home, and less so other parts of the Dreaming, and mages aren\u2019t in tune with anything. Meant was bit of a strong word for that, but yeah, I felt it fit at the time. Still might, though I\u2019d have been right for the wrong reasons.<br /> <br /> Density being the issue certainly tracks with the language of the text\u2026but why? Why would a personal dream be more dense than the bright dream? Is it because it\u2019s coming from one head/soul, instead of all of humanity\u2019s heads/souls? Like the containers are physically smaller? Because otherwise I would have assumed the bright dream was more crowded, because it has all of humanity\u2019s thoughts to sort through.<br /> <br /> So, if it\u2019s based on Density, would the Beast\u2019s discomfort reasonably not be applicable to dreams? I think Changeling says that dreams are mostly Prop, with a few Actors. Seems less likely to make Beast feel claustrophobic.<br /> <br /> I still think role is important, namely I don\u2019t think a Beast merged with the Horror can pick a role besides night terror. I was building up to the idea that if a role is forced on a Beast, if they Primordial Pathways in, they are going to be interpreted as being the Horror by the dream, and expected to do Horror like things. If a Beast is clever, they could avoid it by not entering the dream merged with the Horror, and not immediately twist the dream into a nightmare. Less immediate power over the dream, but more ways to use the power you do have. Now some of that is based on wrong assumptions, but I wonder if I can still work with it?<br /> <br /> Edit:Clarity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-20-2023, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T21:19:06-07:00","id":1509133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509040#post1509040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if it\u2019s based on Density, would the Beast\u2019s discomfort reasonably not be applicable to dreams? I think Changeling says that dreams are mostly Prop, with a few Actors. Seems less likely to make Beast feel claustrophobic.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Temenos, the Realms are made up of the dialogue of shared narratives. &quot;People&quot; are paying attention, but only to the extent that it's more risky/nerve-wracking to do stuff in front of an audience.<br /> <br /> The Oneiros is <i>a place of self-reflection</i>. Everything interacting with a visitor is doing so under the assumption that they're the person whose thoughts created them if they engage from the tableau at all. You're being scrutinized because the Oneiros is where one goes to scrutinize themselves.<br /> <br /> Regular dreams cycle back around to not being as intense by default \u2014 things can be unimportant in oneiromancy based on whether they represent something from the dreamer's mind or are just there for set dressing \u2014 but needing to play a role to accomplish anything in oneiromancy is a pseudo-social thing; you have to steer the scene on its own terms, and that means presenting as something that aligns with what's there already. You have to pose as a visiting archaeologist or a private investigator or a cat burglar to convince the dream to give you information and, without a paradigm shift, you won't get further results by acting outside of the role you've taken up, because the dream won't play along any more than your sports team would if you started acting like a producer for The Bachelor in the middle of a big game \u2014 that's not the story being told by you and the dream at the moment, and the sudden twist hasn't been narratively earned.<br /> <br /> The Primordial Dream is <i>thin</i>. The one consistent unseen observer is (probably) the Dark Mother, in contrast to the press of humanity in the Temenos or the mirrored fixation of the Oneiros; those bits of the Dark Dream that aren't the dreamscape itself carry bits of how the Bright Dream works into the prosaic landscape of the Astral view of the material world as divorced from the directed attention of the world itself and humanity as a whole, with Burrows working the way connections between Bright Realms work, Lairs evoking memories of events that the present has tried to move on from.<br /> <br /> Dreams aren't the inside of the soul. There's no density to worry about there, because you can't walk out of the inside of the soul and getting to regular dreams takes a separate route where intrinsic degrees of scrutiny aren't a metaphysical concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T22:00:13-07:00","id":1509134,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>. <br /> <br /> Ok, so a dream has a narrative. And to mess with it, one has to play along. So what exactly happens when a Horror Pathways inside? I\u2019m guessing it doesn\u2019t have to play along with the existing narrative, it can rampage all it wants or otherwise do it\u2019s thing. Is it doing that by changing what going to happen the the narrative? Or is it overriding the narrative? I guess a better way to phrase it would be: does the Horror technically have a role, when it engages with the dream? If so, a Beast would likely have a similar role if they try to Pathway in. If not, then the Beast is free to engage with the dream on their own terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T22:41:42-07:00","id":1509136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509134#post1509134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so a dream has a narrative. And to mess with it, one has to play along. So what exactly happens when a Horror Pathways inside? I\u2019m guessing it doesn\u2019t have to play along with the existing narrative, it can rampage all it wants or otherwise do it\u2019s thing. Is it doing that by changing what going to happen the the narrative? Or is it overriding the narrative? I guess a better way to phrase it would be: does the Horror technically have a role, when it engages with the dream? If so, a Beast would likely have a similar role if they try to Pathway in. If not, then the Beast is free to engage with the dream on their own terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that Inflicting Nightmares works along the same narrative lines as a larval Horror with streamlined mechanics, the Horror opens a Primordial Pathway in response to dreamed situations that will allow it to feed, probably including the presence of Lair Traits in the scene as well, which means that the narrative of the dream had room for &quot;a monster arrives and asserts dominance/punishes a transgression/steals something/makes you aware that one of your secrets is out/etc,&quot; which the Horror will likely progress the story towards at its preferred pace.<br /> <br /> It's kind of a moot point whether or not a Beast or their Horror &quot;has&quot; a role in a dream, because oneiromancy is not an ability any character who is in a dream is assumed to have \u2014 per the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle, a changeling and a Horror in the same dream use their respective systems for interacting with the dream \u2014 and &quot;playing a role&quot; is Changeling's non-dice-based prerequisite action of &quot;getting stuff out of dreams with oneiromancy requires some give-and-take,&quot; akin to how Astral Realms (pages 40-45) talks about Dream Actors and Affecting Scenes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the dreamer acts out of character, it confuses dream actors. They\u2019re part of a memory where the dreamer is nine and carefree and don\u2019t understand when he says, \u201cI can\u2019t stay here. I\u2019ve gotta find the night Jenny died!\u201d Such events slide from dream actors\u2019 consciousnesses with little impact \u2014 Cousin Jack pauses and might ask who Jenny is, then goes back to talking about getting the Frisbee.\u200b </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A person can affect an Oneiros not her own, if she is clever. The right word in the dreamer\u2019s ear, a recognized smell or a certain sound can all bring certain memories to the fore, just as manipulation of the dreamer\u2019s psyche can dull old mental wounds and make the unconscious gentler. When able to influence the dreamer, either because he is astral and right beside her or because she has accomplices in real space, the character attempting to shift the subconscious needs an exceptional success on a Manipulation + Persuasion, Intimidation or Expression roll. </div> </div> </div>The narrative in a dream does not have a &quot;going to happen&quot; to change except in the sense that some dreams involve revisiting events that have already happened \u2014 the narrative a role exists in is based on established &quot;facts&quot; about the setting of the dream. (You're at a birthday party. You've presented yourself as a police officer. Acting like the birthday clown at this point is just going to confuse people the same as it would if you tried it in real life.) Some actors native to the dream will have supernatural powers enforcing their role in the narrative, but oneiropomps and other visitors are definitionally not those actors \u2014 Changeling 2e has playing roles and the nature of truth as a social construct as recurring parts of its metaphysical activity.<br /> <br /> The need to play a role in oneiromancy is a Watsonian and Doylist justification for why you can't just make the dream do what you want as an abstract exercise, not a script strictly straitjacketing your activity, and a Horror having an impact on the dream by definition has established its role for that purpose, which it does through the systems that Beast uses for interacting with dreams, i.e. normal dice rolls, because Beasts and their Horrors do not use oneiromancy as mechanically presented in Changeling as a tool for changelings, Fae, Huntsmen, and certain fae-touched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-21-2023, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T00:05:47-07:00","id":1509141,"title":"","content":"Wow, ok. That was extremely helpful and answers pretty much every question besides one last holdout. Probably answers the last one too, but I want to be sure.<br /> <br /> Given that Shift Conditions require a paradigm shift, which requires oneiromancy, is it true that Beasts cannot acquire them, no matter how far they warp the dream they are in? Aka, if a Beast decides to say, kill all of the eidolon/dream actors in order to feed, they won't gain a Shift Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T05:23:43-07:00","id":1509168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509141#post1509141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Shift Conditions require a paradigm shift, which requires oneiromancy, is it true that Beasts cannot acquire them, no matter how far they warp the dream they are in? Aka, if a Beast decides to say, kill all of the eidolon/dream actors in order to feed, they won't gain a Shift Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is my understanding, yes.<br /> <br /> Operating from the Bastion itself rather than the inside of the soul means their actions would still be penalized by the dreamer's Composure despite their lack of ability to spend Glamour to effect shifts, but the extent to which the dream will play along is limited to the ways it &quot;thinks&quot; the situation would respond to those actions, rather than your choice of effects from the table.<br /> <br /> Functionally this would be the dreamweaving equivalent of trying to get results in the Hedge solely through prompting it to Hedgespin itself in reaction to what you're doing; Shift Conditions represent you drawing <i>unnatural</i> attention to yourself, as the dream recognizes you're trying to change or extract something below the surface with Glamour and moves to protect the deeper contents of the person.<br /> <br /> I don't believe killing eidolons would allow you to feed any more than you could from smashing a wall in the dreamscape \u2014 they're not real people with a persistent existence outside the dream, so &quot;if someone eats, something gets eaten&quot; doesn't really have stakes in that case \u2014 and killing a dreamer in their own Bastion likewise doesn't even inflict a Condition.<br /> <br /> Basically, a Beast acting in a Bastion through the channels changelings use to get into dreams doesn't really have any especial means of affecting the dreamer more than showing them a dream where the Beast does whatever they're doing; it doesn't serve as a shortcut for them to do stuff like they would in the Oneiros except maybe in the same sense that opening a Primordial Pathway lets you deliberately target you Horror's feeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T10:58:55-07:00","id":1509216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509168#post1509168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">means their actions would still be penalized by the dreamer's Composure despite their lack of ability to spend Glamour to effect shifts</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was under the impression that non dream-weaving rolls didn\u2019t qualify for the penalty. Is that not the case?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure I\u2019m starting to sound like a broken record, but really: Thanks! This all has been super helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T23:12:09-07:00","id":1509256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509216#post1509216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I was under the impression that non dream-weaving rolls didn\u2019t qualify for the penalty. Is that not the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every mundane action in the dream <i>can</i> be used for dreamweaving; if you're not a lucid dreamer with the ability to spend Glamour, you have no ability to leverage the tradeoff for those penalties, but muddling through the narrative of the dream without oneiromancy is specifically possible as a means of finding the exit to the Bastion, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T13:29:20-07:00","id":1509310,"title":"","content":"OK, that's basically everything for a baseline of what happens when a Beast enters a dream. Now, why would a Beast want to? Well, Feeding is always a good motivator. Dreams are probably the best ratio of potential consequences vs potential gain possible, with even the death of the dreamer inside the dream only causing them to wake up. A Beast can go all out, well almost all out, (the penalty to mundane actions still stands) without worrying about the long-term ramifications of the High Satiety feeding. I mean the dreamer might get freaked out a monster burnt down their childhood home, but it was all inside a dream so they should be fine if a bit spooked. If we want to be a bit messed up, the Beast can abduct the dreamer's dream form into their lair, and (assuming their horror doesn't prey on the dreamer) they have made sure the dreamer's body is in a coma. Any enterprising Beast with Doppelganger can probably see the potential, no need for Shrouds of Observation this time. It's also not a bad way to communicate with/manipulate a cult, or hang out with Incubi/Hobs/Changelings for kinship and friendship.<br /> <br /> The main problem is that entering dreams is both unreliable and willpower expensive. I imagine most Beasts interested in messing with dreams would look into ways to mitigate those disadvantages. This might be a decent area for a homebrew Obcasus Rite. Do a ritual to curse the target with nightmares, that provide enough resonance to enter the Bastion with Pathways. A merit building off of Stalking Ground could do something similar, giving easy access to someone's dreams. If nothing else, Feeding on someone is likely to have that event play out again in their dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-22-2023, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T18:21:16-07:00","id":1509425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509310#post1509310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, that's basically everything for a baseline of what happens when a Beast enters a dream. Now, why would a Beast want to? Well, Feeding is always a good motivator. Dreams are probably the best ratio of potential consequences vs potential gain possible, with even the death of the dreamer inside the dream only causing them to wake up. A Beast can go all out, well almost all out, (the penalty to mundane actions still stands) without worrying about the long-term ramifications of the High Satiety feeding. I mean the dreamer might get freaked out a monster burnt down their childhood home, but it was all inside a dream so they should be fine if a bit spooked.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're bodily visiting a victim in a Bastion, you're a person using your normal Attributes or (if you somehow manage to thread the needle of getting to the Dreaming Roads from the Astral outside your Lair) a Dream Form based on your Mental Attributes. The monster is the Horror, who stays in the Lair without the technicality of overlapping into your location for a few turns to a scene.<br /> <br /> The death of the dreamer is also very bad news for any visitors, because that means the Bastion's gone and you're getting dropped in a functionally random location in the cosmology. It also seems highly optimistic to assume the only consequences the dreamer will experience are waking up just because the Begotten don't have the native ability to spend Glamour to e.g. inflict the Ravaged Condition on a dreamer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we want to be a bit messed up, the Beast can abduct the dreamer's dream form into their lair, and (assuming their horror doesn't prey on the dreamer) they have made sure the dreamer's body is in a coma. Any enterprising Beast with Doppelganger can probably see the potential, no need for Shrouds of Observation this time. It's also not a bad way to communicate with/manipulate a cult, or hang out with Incubi/Hobs/Changelings for kinship and friendship. </div> </div> </div>The Horror dragging a victim's Dream Form into the Lair is the result of an exceptional success on the Inflicting Nightmares roll, where it attempts to &quot;kill&quot; the dreamer, which is in line with what it normally does with intruders if left to its own devices. A character in Dream Form who is killed returns to their body with the Soul Shocked Condition.<br /> <br /> Communicating with a cult is likewise better managed by meeting in person or using magic or technology that doesn't rely on the recipient of your message remembering the contents of their dreams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main problem is that entering dreams is both unreliable and willpower expensive. I imagine most Beasts interested in messing with dreams would look into ways to mitigate those disadvantages. This might be a decent area for a homebrew Obcasus Rite. Do a ritual to curse the target with nightmares, that provide enough resonance to enter the Bastion with Pathways. A merit building off of Stalking Ground could do something similar, giving easy access to someone's dreams. If nothing else, Feeding on someone is likely to have that event play out again in their dreams. </div> </div> </div>I am moderately certain that outgoing Pathways to people's dreams are not going to land in the Bastion, between Pathways to the Hedge coming out on the Dreaming Roads and Bastions contesting attempts to break in even without the intervention of an eidolon (when the fringes of a dream bring dreamweaving mechanics into play and the average mortal is penalizing rolls by two dice while contesting with either two dice or the stats of a Wyrd 2 eidolon).<br /> <br /> Just as Beast can't be an obvious solution to the problems Demon presents, Changeling's metaphysics cannot provide a blatant avenue for ignoring the core premise of Beast as a game. Family Dinners with accompanying nightmares is well and good, but &quot;I can shortcut past the things making dreams a source of indirect access to the soul <i>and</i> gain meaningful sustenance from direct feeding there without significant consequence&quot; doesn't feel like it should fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T19:27:13-07:00","id":1509427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509425#post1509425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're bodily visiting a victim in a Bastion, you're a person using your normal Attributes or (if you somehow manage to thread the needle of getting to the Dreaming Roads from the Astral outside your Lair) a Dream Form based on your Mental Attributes. The monster is the Horror, who stays in the Lair without the technicality of overlapping into your location for a few turns to a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. I was including that technicality in going all out. Sorry if that wasn't clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509425#post1509425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The death of the dreamer is also very bad news for any visitors, because that means the Bastion's gone and you're getting dropped in a functionally random location in the cosmology. It also seems highly optimistic to assume the only consequences the dreamer will experience are waking up just because the Begotten don't have the native ability to spend Glamour to e.g. inflict the Ravaged Condition on a dreamer.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, but Beasts have Pathways back. They would probably care less about collapsing a Bastion than a Changeling/Hob who can't pop back into a safe location. (Plus I think it's kinda on brand that Nightmare Shamans wouldn't care about Nightmares waking people up, even if it inconveniences them.) A secondary concern is that if the Beast feeds, a dreamer will remember it exceptionally clearly for a dream. Which might be a problem without some measures to hide themselves. (I'm basing this on the Horror inflicting Nightmares which the victims remember clearly. I think it would be fair to argue the victim also loses a willpower, like when the Horror just has a normal success.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509425#post1509425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Horror dragging a victim's Dream Form into the Lair is the result of an exceptional success on the Inflicting Nightmares roll, where it attempts to &quot;kill&quot; the dreamer, which is in line with what it normally does with intruders if left to its own devices. A character in Dream Form who is killed returns to their body with the Soul Shocked Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, which is where I got the idea from, but with the Beast directing things, they could hypothetically manage to imprison them instead of killing them. While I don't know for certain if the dreamer can't wake up from inside the Lair, they are no longer in the Dreaming Roads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509425#post1509425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Communicating with a cult is likewise better managed by meeting in person or using magic or technology that doesn't rely on the recipient of your message remembering the contents of their dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div> True. I don't think Beasts have easy access to any other magic that works for long-distance communication that doesn't need a person to be at a specific location.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509425#post1509425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am moderately certain that outgoing Pathways to people's dreams are not going to land in the Bastion, between Pathways to the Hedge coming out on the Dreaming Roads and Bastions contesting attempts to break in even without the intervention of an eidolon (when the fringes of a dream bring dreamweaving mechanics into play and the average mortal is penalizing rolls by two dice while contesting with either two dice or the stats of a Wyrd 2 eidolon).</div> </div> </div> </div>...That's a pretty important difference. I guess that interpretation seems weird to me? I mean, I don't think the Horror wanders the Dreaming Roads before entering a Bastion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509425#post1509425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as Beast can't be an obvious solution to the problems Demon presents, Changeling's metaphysics cannot provide a blatant avenue for ignoring the core premise of Beast as a game. Family Dinners with accompanying nightmares is well and good, but &quot;I can shortcut past the things making dreams a source of indirect access to the soul <i>and</i> gain meaningful sustenance from direct feeding there without significant consequence&quot; doesn't feel like it should fly.</div> </div> </div> </div> A fair argument. Though I'd argue that this particular line of reasoning exists in Beast's conceptual space even without Changeling's metaphysics. (If the Horror can go there, why can't I? Especially with Pathways reaching all sorts of weird places.) So, what do you suggest? Heroic Tracking could be a consequence. Could be a Bastion has unique deterrents for Beasts. Maybe the Bastion makes feeding harder, since on some level, it doesn't have the long-reaching consequences Feeding normally has. I was leaning towards the narrative effect of eidolon's being naturally hostile to the Beast, much like with the Shift Conditions, due to the nature of being a night terror manifesting in a dream, but I think you pointed out that wouldn't happen due to the differences in how Beasts engage with a Dream vs Changelings. Maybe I could look back into to that?<br /> <br /> Edit: 4 willpower at minimum is quite the investment. I\u2019d also argue the Pathways roll gets the penalties for being in the Hedge (duh), and technically being a non specific location, since as I understand, it\u2019s a new location every time. Now one can probably fulfill Legend or Life in a Bastion, but that upfront cost is definitely a major mitigating factor. Should I not pursue cost reduction merits and the like in order to preserve that \u201cFeeding\u201d theme of Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-23-2023, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T22:03:27-07:00","id":1509445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509427#post1509427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but Beasts have Pathways back.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Pathways have prerequisites that rely on their linking up with your Lair. Even if you don't subscribe to the reading I have that requires the external end of the Pathway to align with a Chamber, you're still looking for at least a Lair Trait from your list before you can think about getting back to familiar ground.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yep, which is where I got the idea from, but with the Beast directing things, they could hypothetically manage to imprison them instead of killing them. While I don't know for certain if the dreamer can't wake up from inside the Lair, they are no longer in the Dreaming Roads. </div> </div> </div>You have to dedicate conscious attention to keeping your Horror from following its own inclinations. A Beast's Lair is her Horror's favored hunting grounds, and without the expenditure of Satiety to tap someone as a guest or merge Lairs as a brood its status as a territorial nightmare creature makes its inclination toward strangers clear. At the point where you're devoting your constant attention to keeping your personal nightmare from finishing off the dream-self of some poor comatose sap in the name of keeping them around to torment without external consequence, I think this stops being about expediency, practicality, or moral alternatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...That's a pretty important difference. I guess that interpretation seems weird to me? I mean, I don't think the Horror wanders the Dreaming Roads before entering a Bastion? </div> </div> </div>The Horror also doesn't have to know where it's going to open a Pathway to someone that will allow it to feed, and is entering the dream through the Astral \u2014 and thus affecting the dreamer at a deeper level \u2014 rather than through the Bastion at the shallow end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A fair argument. Though I'd argue that this particular line of reasoning exists in Beast's conceptual space even without Changeling's metaphysics. (If the Horror can go there, why can't I? Especially with Pathways reaching all sorts of weird places.) </div> </div> </div>See above; the Horror is in the Bastion by virtue of being in the dream, but it interacts with the dream with its normal systems rather than <i>as a Bastion</i>. The Horror doesn't know the difference, and if you're trying to get to the layer on top of the &quot;Now Playing&quot; zone of the personal soul you don't have that instinctual ignorance to go off of. At best you'd land on the fringes of the dream in the Dreaming Roads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, what do you suggest? Heroic Tracking could be a consequence. Could be a Bastion has unique deterrents for Beasts. Maybe the Bastion makes feeding harder, since on some level, it doesn't have the long-reaching consequences Feeding normally has. I was leaning towards the narrative effect of eidolon's being naturally hostile to the Beast, much like with the Shift Conditions, due to the nature of being a night terror manifesting in a dream, but I think you pointed out that wouldn't happen due to the differences in how Beasts engage with a Dream vs Changelings. Maybe I could look back into to that? </div> </div> </div>Feeding as yourself instead of letting the Horror do it requires the dreamer experience the shock of realizing what is happening, which is difficult to manage when they aren't conscious and you aren't visibly presenting as a monster; halving the successes on the feeding roll (rounding down) as though you'd spent Willpower to force Satiety processing before the end of the scene is as much of a compromise as I'd offer for working through that kind of filter \u2014 like with the Oneiros, the principal benefit I'd extend to going so far out of your way is the capacity to target your Horror's next victim when it's Starving.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, the point at which a Beast can comfortably use frequent and/or protracted extradimensional voyages as a source of regular Satiety is the point at which they have stopped being connected enough to the human sphere to not have undergone an Inheritance or stranger transformations. Exploration of the wider world is generally for meeting the Kinship side of the scale, not Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T20:48:00-07:00","id":1509551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509445#post1509445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Pathways have prerequisites that rely on their linking up with your Lair. Even if you don't subscribe to the reading I have that requires the external end of the Pathway to align with a Chamber, you're still looking for at least a Lair Trait from your list before you can think about getting back to familiar ground.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. My reading is that it works even on places that are the same type of place as a chamber one has, even without Traits, which must be insanely liberal from your point of view. Might need a sanity checker on that. Anyways, Traits can be imposed on a dream, and may be the thing that allows access in the first place. I'd imagine a Beast makes sure the dream is to their advantage before going in. It's a safety net. Maybe not a perfect one, but it does provide a way back. It's going to affect how Beasts interact with dreams, and make them more relaxed about waking the dreamer. It's also a rug that can be pulled out from under them if things go sufficiently wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509445#post1509445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to dedicate conscious attention to keeping your Horror from following its own inclinations. A Beast's Lair is her Horror's favored hunting grounds, and without the expenditure of Satiety to tap someone as a guest or merge Lairs as a brood its status as a territorial nightmare creature makes its inclination toward strangers clear. At the point where you're devoting your constant attention to keeping your personal nightmare from finishing off the dream-self of some poor comatose sap in the name of keeping them around to torment without external consequence, I think this stops being about expediency, practicality, or moral alternatives.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah. I'm tending toward closing this particular line of thought because it gets more messed up the more details come up. If someone else wants to explore it, that's on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509445#post1509445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Horror also doesn't have to know where it's going to open a Pathway to someone that will allow it to feed, and is entering the dream through the Astral \u2014 and thus affecting the dreamer at a deeper level \u2014 rather than through the Bastion at the shallow end.</div> </div> </div> </div> Technically, neither does a Beast if I'm interpreting that -3 penalty for only specifying a world, and not a place in it correctly.<br /> <br /> Is there any particular reason outside of it currently not having a system that a Beast couldn't learn to do the same? Entering through the Astral, I mean. That way we can ignore the rest of Changeling's metaphysics, and lean more on Beast's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509445#post1509445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See above; the Horror is in the Bastion by virtue of being in the dream, but it interacts with the dream with its normal systems rather than <i>as a Bastion</i>. The Horror doesn't know the difference, and if you're trying to get to the layer on top of the &quot;Now Playing&quot; zone of the personal soul you don't have that instinctual ignorance to go off of. At best you'd land on the fringes of the dream in the Dreaming Roads.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean...would a Beast know either? They might see it as a temporary zone, like a lesser part of the Dreaming that is only accessible for a moment. Considering how they interact with most systems of the dream, I doubt anyone would think it was part of a wider whole, and go looking for a door out. Since it's a lot harder to go the Dreaming Roads, especially if the penalty for not being an exact location applies, maybe Beasts in general don't think it's possible to go directly to the dream, inside preferring to go through the Astral side if that's possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509445#post1509445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeding as yourself instead of letting the Horror do it requires the dreamer experience the shock of realizing what is happening, which is difficult to manage when they aren't conscious and you aren't visibly presenting as a monster; halving the successes on the feeding roll (rounding down) as though you'd spent Willpower to force Satiety processing before the end of the scene is as much of a compromise as I'd offer for working through that kind of filter \u2014 like with the Oneiros, the principal benefit I'd extend to going so far out of your way is the capacity to target your Horror's next victim when it's Starving.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, ok. There are plenty of Watsonian reasons why it would work that way, and helping preserve Beast's themes certainly isn't a bad Doylist reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509445#post1509445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broadly speaking, the point at which a Beast can comfortably use frequent and/or protracted extradimensional voyages as a source of regular Satiety is the point at which they have stopped being connected enough to the human sphere to not have undergone an Inheritance or stranger transformations. Exploration of the wider world is generally for meeting the Kinship side of the scale, not Hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough. I think I remember several examples of hanging out in various otherworlds, but that was always through the lens of Kinship, as you have noted.<br /> <br /> One new thing to bring up is apparently the Poster who started the fan-made Night Horror that started this thread desires to have rules for Changelings exploring the Primordial Dream. Outside of an Obcasus rite to have a permanent portal between the Hedge and the Dream, is there a way to facilitate that?<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T05:05:21-07:00","id":1509574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1508831-alpen-mares-and-sleep-paralysis-dream-metaphysics-in-beast?p=1509551#post1509551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yep. My reading is that it works even on places that are the same type of place as a chamber one has, even without Traits, which must be insanely liberal from your point of view. Might need a sanity checker on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has actually been <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1305137-unpacking-the-lair\">my main reading</a> for most of the gameline's existence, with the main wrinkle being the Player's Guide saying that opening a Pathway back to the Lair from the Bright Dream is &quot;as easy as&quot; finding a Realm whose Theme matches a Lair Trait.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Technically, neither does a Beast if I'm interpreting that -3 penalty for only specifying a world, and not a place in it correctly.<br /> <br /> Is there any particular reason outside of it currently not having a system that a Beast couldn't learn to do the same? Entering through the Astral, I mean. That way we can ignore the rest of Changeling's metaphysics, and lean more on Beast's. </div> </div> </div>The system for doing that is going to the Oneiros, in this case entering the aforementioned &quot;Now Playing&quot; part of the personal soul where one's active thoughts and dreams play out, which subjects anyone in it for longer than a scene to the Dreamquake Tilt. Larval Horrors open a Pathway there instinctively and ignore the penalty normally applied by the Oneiros.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean...would a Beast know either? They might see it as a temporary zone, like a lesser part of the Dreaming that is only accessible for a moment. Considering how they interact with most systems of the dream, I doubt anyone would think it was part of a wider whole, and go looking for a door out. Since it's a lot harder to go the Dreaming Roads, especially if the penalty for not being an exact location applies, maybe Beasts in general don't think it's possible to go directly to the dream, inside preferring to go through the Astral side if that's possible. </div> </div> </div>Beasts know when they're in the Astral and when they aren't, because they can feel which way their Lair is and literally physically travel to it. Per the &quot;The Call of Home&quot; sidebar in the BPG:<br /> <br /> &quot;This uncanny homing sense also serves as a warning when a Beast really wanders off the beaten track \u2014 it only functions within the Astral Realms, so a Beast who follows a Primordial Pathway out into an unknown part of the universe is instantly aware that she isn\u2019t in the Dream or its neighbors any more. That the homing sense doesn\u2019t work in the Hedge tells Beasts exploring Kinship with changelings that while they may both explore dreams and nightmares, wherever the fae escaped from isn\u2019t in the Dream.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One new thing to bring up is apparently the Poster who started the fan-made Night Horror that started this thread desires to have rules for Changelings exploring the Primordial Dream. Outside of an Obcasus rite to have a permanent portal between the Hedge and the Dream, is there a way to facilitate that? </div> </div> </div>The Dukhan vampire clan from One Thousand and One Nightmares in Dark Eras 2 has a Devotion that allows them to project their consciousness into the Primordial Dream through an unclaimed Chamber with Lair Traits in common with their current location; given that &quot;Sometimes, a great and powerful beast crosses the path on its way down roads where the Fae cannot follow&quot; is an actual line from the Dreaming Roads' writeup, a case could be made for a Contract or a Merit modifying a Contract to allow a changeling to use a limited form of Hedge navigation off the path in the Dreaming Roads to reach a Chamber that's part of a hive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}